# VLM2Vec Training Workflow

## Core Training Components

### Main Entry Points
- [train.py](mdc:train.py) - Main training script entry point
- [experiments/public/train/train_v2-qwen2vl-2B.sh](mdc:experiments/public/train/train_v2-qwen2vl-2B.sh) - Training shell script with key parameters

### Model Architecture
- [src/model/model.py](mdc:src/model/model.py) - Core MMEBModel class implementing contrastive learning
- [src/model/processor.py](mdc:src/model/processor.py) - Multi-modal input processing for different backbones

### Data Processing Pipeline
- [src/data/loader/mixed_dataset.py](mdc:src/data/loader/mixed_dataset.py) - Multi-dataset interleaving logic
- [src/data/collator/train_collator.py](mdc:src/data/collator/train_collator.py) - Multi-modal data collation
- [src/data/dataset/mmeb_dataset.py](mdc:src/data/dataset/mmeb_dataset.py) - MMEB dataset processing

### Training Infrastructure
- [src/trainer.py](mdc:src/trainer.py) - GradCacheLateProcessTrainer with distributed training support
- [src/loss.py](mdc:src/loss.py) - Contrastive loss implementations
- [src/arguments.py](mdc:src/arguments.py) - Training configuration arguments

### Configuration Files
- [experiments/public/train/train_alltasks.yaml](mdc:experiments/public/train/train_alltasks.yaml) - Dataset mixing configuration
- [requirements.txt](mdc:requirements.txt) - Dependencies and versions

## Key Training Parameters
- LoRA: `--lora --lora_r 16`
- Model: `--model_name Qwen/Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct`
- Pooling: `--pooling eos --normalize True`
- Temperature: `--temperature 0.02`
- Gradient Cache: `--grad_cache True`
- Batch Size: `--per_device_train_batch_size 128`
- Learning Rate: `--learning_rate 5e-5`

## Data Types Supported
1. Image-Text pairs (MMEB-train datasets)
2. Video-Text pairs (LLaVA-Hound)
3. Visual Document pairs (Vidore, VisRAG)

## Training Tips
- Use gradient caching for large batch training
- Interleave different datasets with weights
- Support checkpoint resumption with `--resume_from auto`
- Monitor training with WandB integration
